# Local reference material — pulled, not authored. Never committed.
.reference/

# Scratch
*.log
.DS_Store

# Secrets — never committed. Values live here; only names go in environment.md.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Orchestrator slice worktrees — branches, not content
.claude/worktrees/

# Python build and cache artefacts. MAP-2 is the first Python in this repo, so these
# arrive with it.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Agent scratch space. Never linted, never committed: a subagent staging a probe in the
# repo root would otherwise fail `test_ruff_passes_over_the_whole_tree`, which lints the
# whole tree by design and cannot tell a probe from a source file.
.tmp-*/

# Same reason, for a probe staged as a file rather than a directory. No source file in this
# tree is a root-level dotfile — `[tool.mypy] files` names src/tests/migrations and nothing
# else — so a root-level `.something.py` is scratch by construction. `.map54_rerun.py`, left
# by a live implementer, failed `ruff format --check` on the whole-tree gate.
/.[!.]*.py

# Terraform working state. `.terraform/` is the downloaded provider -- hundreds of MB
# for hashicorp/aws alone. The state files hold the account's resource metadata, and
# git does not forget: committing one publishes it into history where deleting the
# file does not remove it. `.terraform.lock.hcl` is NOT here and is committed on
# purpose -- it pins the provider version and its checksums, which is what makes two
# people's plans comparable.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform.tfstate.lock.info
tfplan

# The design record. Untracked on purpose, and still on disk: `docs/`, `CONTEXT.md` and
# `STATE.md` are how the work here is planned, decided and remembered, and they are read
# every session. None of it is part of what somebody deploying or extending this platform
# needs, and some of it names internal accounts, incidents and working assumptions that
# should not leave with the source.
#
# Ignoring alone would have done nothing -- every one of these was tracked, and a
# `.gitignore` entry has no effect on a file git already follows. They were removed from
# the index with `git rm --cached`, which is what these lines then keep out.
#
# History still holds them, so a push of this branch's history publishes what these lines
# withhold from its tip. `tools/publish.py` is the answer to that: one squashed snapshot,
# one tree, exactly what `--dry-run` prints.
docs/
CONTEXT.md
STATE.md

# The agent pipeline's own instructions. Not secret -- but every pointer in them resolves
# into `docs/`, so beside a tree with no `docs/` they are a page of dangling references,
# which is worse than their absence.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
.claude/

# The one test that reads the design record: it asserts every skip gate in the suite
# appears in `docs/test-gates.md`. With that document untracked the test fails a clone for
# the absence of a file rather than for anything about the code, so it leaves with what it
# grades. The gate table itself is reproduced in README.md, which is where a reader
# outside this repository looks for it.
tests/test_gates.py

# The two spike guards that read the spike record itself. They assert the Verdict is one
# of three permitted strings and that no Measured row is blank -- properties of a document
# under `docs/`, not of any code here. With that document untracked they fail a clone at
# `pytest.fail("the spike record does not exist at ...")`, which is what a CI runner
# reported on the first push. `test_spike_image.py` stays: it reads `deploy/spike`, builds
# the image, and grades two binaries in it.
tests/spike/test_record_complete.py
tests/spike/test_report_shape.py

# Terraform's account-specific inputs. The configuration derives the account id from the
# caller's own credentials (`deploy/terraform/account.tf`), so almost nothing needs to be
# configured -- but a backend block takes no expressions, so the state bucket's name
# arrives through `-backend-config`. `.example` files beside these carry the shape.
deploy/terraform/backend.hcl
*.tfvars
